[
    {
        "content": "<p>As part of an effort to generalize <code>MultilinearMap</code>to allow for semilinear maps there is an opportunity to introduce notation analogous to those already in place for <code>(Continuous)LinearMap</code>, <code>ContinuousMultilinearMap</code> and <code>AlternatingMap</code>.<br>\nMy proposal for multilinear maps (see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43877\">#43877</a>) is</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>M →ₘₗ[R] N</code> for <code>MultilinearMap R M N</code>, mirroring the notation <code>M →ₗ[R] N</code> for <code>LinearMap R M N</code>.</li>\n<li><code>M [×n]→ₗ[R] N</code> for <code>MultilinearMap R (fun _ : Fin n =&gt; M) N</code>, mirroring the notation <code>M [×n]→L[R] N</code> for <code>ContinuousMultilinearMap R (fun _ : Fin n =&gt; M) N</code>.</li>\n<li><code>M [^ι]→ₗ[R] N</code> for <code>MultilinearMap R (fun _ : ι =&gt; M) N</code>, mirroring the notation <code>M [⋀^ι]→ₗ[R] N</code> for <code>AlternatingMap R M N ι</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>and when generalized to multi-semilinear maps (to be added to <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42534\">#42534</a>) also</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>M →ₘₛₗ[σ] N</code></li>\n<li><code>M [×n]→ₛₗ[σ] N</code></li>\n<li><code>M [^ι]→ₛₗ[σ] N</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Do these look okay? Any suggestions to improve these or entirely different notation schemes to consider? Personally I'm not thrilled with the \"<code>[^ι]→</code>\" for a general non-dependent type...</p>",
        "id": 625332817,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1789762110
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The second is obviously fine since it mirrors the continuous version.<br>\nThe first and third are the real ones to discuss</p>",
        "id": 625333763,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1789762435
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wonder if we can just have a single notation though (like the first) and then if you want to do the second and third you can just write <code>(fun _ : Fin n =&gt; M) →ₘₗ[R] N</code> and <code>(fun _ : ι =&gt; M) →ₘₗ[R] N</code></p>",
        "id": 625336451,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1789763298
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"477483\">Monica Omar</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Notation.20for.20.60MultilinearMap.60/near/625336451\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>if you want to do the second and third you can just write <code>(fun _ : Fin n =&gt; M) →ₘₗ[R] N</code> and <code>(fun _ : ι =&gt; M) →ₘₗ[R] N</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I agree with this. A cleaner solution may be to have a good notation for <code>(fun _ : Fin n =&gt; M)</code> / <code>(fun _ : ι =&gt; M) </code> (for example <code>M^⊕ι</code>) and then use the <code>→ₘₗ[R]</code> notation everywhere instead of having seperate cases for the <code>`(fun _ : Fin n =&gt; M)</code> / <code>(fun _ : ι =&gt; M) </code> cases.</p>",
        "id": 625339449,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1789764334
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Older discussion at <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Notation.20for.20.60multilinear_map.60/near/225694500\">#general &gt; Notation for &#96;multilinear_map&#96; @ 💬</a></p>",
        "id": 625349887,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1789768964
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Notation.20for.20.60MultilinearMap.60/near/625349887\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Older discussion at <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Notation.20for.20.60multilinear_map.60/near/225694500\">#general &gt; Notation for &#96;multilinear_map&#96; @ 💬</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I see that for mathlib3 the proposal was <code>→ₗₘ</code> so that the continuous version could be <code>→Lₘ</code>.<br>\nThinking ahead maybe <code>→ₗₘ/→ₛₗₘ</code> is better to adopt than <code>→ₘₗ/→ₘₛₗ</code> since when it comes time for notation for continuous multilinear maps <code>→Lₘ/→SLₘ</code> seems preferable over <code>→ML/→MSL</code> or <code>→ₘL/→ₘSL</code> (at least to me).</p>",
        "id": 625360282,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1789775327
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>→ₗₘ/→ₛₗₘ</code> and <code>→Lₘ/→SLₘ</code> seem fine to me</p>",
        "id": 626439258,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1790194928
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43877\">#43877</a> has been updated to just use the <code>M →ₗₘ[R] N</code> notation everywhere.</p>",
        "id": 627002731,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1790372773
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think my only concern with this notation is that newcomers might think <code>lm</code> stands for linear map rather than multi-linear. But maybe that's not too big of an issue</p>",
        "id": 627083662,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1790422970
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>/poll notation for multilinear maps<br>\n<code>→ₗₘ/→ₛₗₘ</code> (so that the continuous versions can be <code>→Lₘ/→SLₘ</code>)<br>\n<code>→ₘₗ/→ₘₛₗ</code> the continuous versions can be (<code>→ML/→MSL</code> or <code>→ₘL/→ₘSL</code> or something else)</p>",
        "id": 631465466,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1791930642
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This didn't seem decided i this thread, so I started the poll above (with terrible parentheses <span aria-label=\"face palm\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f926\" role=\"img\" title=\"face palm\">:face_palm:</span>). I would like to merge the PR soon, so I hope to come to a consensus quickly.</p>",
        "id": 631465602,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1791930704
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't like <code>ₗₘ</code> because to me it reads like \"Linear Map\", but what it really means is \"Linear Multi\", which is out of order. Personally, I think <code>ML</code> and <code>MSL</code>  would be fine (note: we are already uppercasing the <code>S</code> there!)</p>",
        "id": 631465831,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1791930785
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Raising something from the ancient Lean 3 thread: right now the rule is that to get to the unbundle version of a notation you drop the symbol, sending all of (<code>A →+ B</code>, <code>A →* B</code>, <code>A →ₗ[R] B</code>) to <code>A → B</code>.</p>\n<p>This proposal does not match this pattern; the bundled version of <code>(Π i, M i) → N</code> is spelt <code>(fun i =&gt; M i) →ₗₘ[R] N</code>, the bundled version of <code>(I → M) → N</code> is spelt <code>(fun _ : I =&gt; M) →ₗₘ[R] N</code>.</p>\n<p>Up to the letter reordering above, should the notation instead be <code>(Π i, M i) →ₗₘ N</code> and <code>(I → M) →ₗₘ N</code> (edit: poll below)?</p>",
        "id": 631531507,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1791954054
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(I think a fairly simple elaborator can safely implement this)</p>",
        "id": 631531951,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1791954253
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>Implementaton</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrettyPrinter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Delaborator</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubExpr</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Eta-reduce `fun (x : dom) =&gt; f x` to `f` when `f` has the same `BinderInfo` and domain `dom`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">etaReduce</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withLocalDecl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">etaReduce</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instantiate1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">abstract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">app</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bvar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hasLooseBVar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lowerLooseBVars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">forallE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fDom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fBi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">whnfR</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fBi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instantiateMVars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fDom</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cleanupAnnotations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cleanupAnnotations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">updateLambdaE!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"pi_to_lam% \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">elab_rules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pi_to_lam</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">whnfR</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">forallE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eM</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throwErrorAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"expected a function or Pi type, got{indentExpr eM}\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">etaReduce</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bi</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">notation</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">25</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\" →ₗₘ[\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">25</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"] \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MultilinearMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pi_to_lam</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">app_delab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MultilinearMap</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delabMultilinearMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Delab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">whenPPOption</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getPPNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getExpr</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">guard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isAppOfArity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``MultilinearMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">9</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withNaryArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withNaryArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">piExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">forallE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bi</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">forallE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getArg!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">app</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">liftLooseBVars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bvar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">default</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">withTheReader</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cfg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cfg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">piExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withNaryArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tests</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: ((i : ι) → M i) →ₗₘ[R] N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: ((i : ι) → M i) →ₗₘ[R] N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Eta-reduced to `MultilinearMap R M N` (not `fun i =&gt; M i`)</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: MultilinearMap R M N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"kn\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: (I → M') →ₗₘ[R] N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: MultilinearMap R (fun a =&gt; M') N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"kn\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: ((i : ι) → M i × N) →ₗₘ[R] N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Bare `MultilinearMap R M N` delaborates to `((i : ι) → M i) →ₗₘ[R] N`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: ((i : ι) → M i) →ₗₘ[R] N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MultilinearMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Right-associative chaining</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: (I → M') →ₗₘ[R] ((i : ι) → M i) →ₗₘ[R] N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Unfolds reducible `abbrev` on the LHS</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: (I → M') →ₗₘ[R] N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Preserves explicit `abbrev` domain distinct from `M`'s domain instead of eta-reducing</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyIdx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: MultilinearMap R (fun i =&gt; M i) N : Type -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"kn\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyIdx</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Error on non-Pi LHS</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: expected a function or Pi type, got</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  N</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗₘ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tests</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>",
        "id": 631553321,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1791961735
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"197836\">Jireh Loreaux</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Notation.20for.20.60MultilinearMap.60/near/631465602\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This didn't seem decided i this thread, so I started the poll above (with terrible parentheses <span aria-label=\"face palm\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f926\" role=\"img\" title=\"face palm\">:face_palm:</span>). I would like to merge the PR soon, so I hope to come to a consensus quickly.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Thanks! I've updated <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43877\">#43877</a> to reflect the overwhelming consensus.</p>",
        "id": 633021081,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1792419683
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>/poll Should we adjust the notation to make the domain look like a function type?</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Yes, the syntax should be <code>(Π i, M i) →ₘₗ N</code> and <code>(I → M) →ₘₗ N</code></li>\n<li>No, the syntax should be <code>(fun i =&gt; M i) →ₘₗ[R] N</code> and <code>(fun _ : I =&gt; M) →ₘₗ N</code></li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 633047783,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1792424856
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My preference for the former is marginal.</p>",
        "id": 633054609,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1792426177
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Seems like as good a time as any to make this change.<br>\nDoes using the pi-type offer any advantage beyond following the (un)bundling convention?</p>",
        "id": 633132377,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1792443727
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>note that we decided to switch from the forall syntax to a function in <code>match (motive := ...)</code></p>",
        "id": 633133141,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1792443937
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1017284\">Gregory Loges</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Notation.20for.20.60MultilinearMap.60/near/633132377\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Seems like as good a time as any to make this change.<br>\nDoes using the pi-type offer any advantage beyond following the (un)bundling convention?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The advantages are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>It matches the expectation set by the unbundling convention</li>\n<li>For non-free-variable indices, it is shorter</li>\n<li>It somewhat matches other syntaxes like  those for<code>Exists</code> and <code>DirectSum</code>, which also do the job of hiding the <code>fun</code> binder.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>and the downsides:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>for free-variable indicies, it is longer</li>\n<li>it has to decide between encouraging users to use an eta expansion of a free-variable, or do some slightly magic eta-reduction behind the scenes</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 633134004,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1792444199
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"477483\">@Monica Omar</span> I don't understand why you're suggesting to mix and match?</p>",
        "id": 633149937,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1792449453
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Because I’m not entirely sure how I feel about <code>I -&gt; M</code> instead of <code>fun _ : I =&gt; M</code>. It’s most probably that I’m not used to it, so forget about my suggestion</p>",
        "id": 633150567,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1792449689
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'll aim to make the change in syntax later today based on the above poll <span aria-label=\"point up\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f446\" role=\"img\" title=\"point up\">:point_up:</span> <br>\nI'm not familiar with elaborators so please forgive my basic questions!</p>\n<ul>\n<li>What (if anything) from the code snippet by <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"310045\">@Eric Wieser</span> should be incorporated into <code>LinearAlgebra/Multilinear/Basic.lean</code>?</li>\n<li>Should the type of <code>MultilinearMap.tofun</code> be changed from <code>(∀ i, M₁ i) → M₂</code> to <code>(Π i, M₁ i) → M₂</code>?</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 633399959,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1792518634
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'll let Eric respond to the first point. But regarding:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>(∀ i, M₁ i) → M₂</code> to <code>(Π i, M₁ i) → M₂</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>These are the same thing (and we are not particularly picky about which one we select).</p>",
        "id": 633400869,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1792518796
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Okay, thanks, I will leave it as-is then <span aria-label=\"slight smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f642\" role=\"img\" title=\"slight smile\">:slight_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 633401922,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1792518983
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I usually suggest <strong>new</strong> statements to say <code>Π i, M i</code> instead of <code>∀ i, M i</code><br>\n(see <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Convention.20for.20.E2.88.80.20vs.2E.20.CE.A0/with/610706777\">#mathlib4 &gt; Convention for ∀ vs. Π</a> for more on this)</p>",
        "id": 633405724,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1792519732
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But yeah, in this case, since you're just editing existing code, I wouldn't change them</p>",
        "id": 633405972,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1792519791
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't claim the elaborator above was perfect; it was written mostly by an agent, with prompting to perform eta reduction and to first create an intermediate <code>pi_to_lam%</code> helper. I suspect it's pretty close to what we want, and a <code>t-meta</code> reviewer (either me or someone else) can help align it with what we actually want.</p>",
        "id": 633415907,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1792522138
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've updated <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43877\">#43877</a> to use <code>(Π i, M i) →ₗₘ[R] N</code> and <code>(ι → M) →ₗₘ[R] N</code> throughout. I think I've caught all of the places in the docs that need updating to reflect the new notation, but I will have another look through everything in the morning.</p>",
        "id": 633826755,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Loges",
        "timestamp": 1792634909
    }
]